  "id": "design-and-behavior",
  "term": "design and behavior",
  "definition": "In this context, design and behavior refers to the features of a robot’s appearance and actions, such as how its eyes move or make contact, that can shape how a person perceives and responds to it socially. These elements may affect whether human-robot interaction is processed more like interaction with another person.",
